{
  "title": "A heater on a stack, cooled by a cold plate",
  "shows": "Heat released on a face (the heater's top, 5 W) flows down a copper stack with a thin, poorly conducting layer to a cold plate whose underside is held at 20 °C: a thermal condition on a side of the domain only solid touches. Still air around it. The energy balance closes, and the stack runs about 13 K above the plate (P·L/(k·A) across the 2 mm layer is 10.7 K).",
